WEBVTT

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:04.966
[Narrator] Welcome to Module 4 Accessible PDF Documents.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.633
In this video, you will learn how to make your PDF

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.966
documents accessible to all learners.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.733
In this section, we will set the PDF's document title

00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:17.866
and language.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.366
As with Word and PowerPoint, PDFs need

00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:23.432
a descriptive title and language setting for

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:24.433
accessibility.

00:00:25.466 --> 00:00:28.266
To set a document title in Adobe PDF,

00:00:28.266 --> 00:00:32.932
click Menu, then select Document Properties.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.433
Locate the Description section. Click on the space

00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:40.766
indicated to the right of Title.

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:44.899
Enter a descriptive title here, such as

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.533
"Teaching Students About Self Efficacy."

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.499
Click OK to apply your settings.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.900
To set the document language, right-click on the document;

00:00:57.366 --> 00:00:59.199
select Document Properties.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.600
Click Advanced, and under Reading Options

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.466
to the right of language, select English,

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.532
and then click OK to apply your settings.

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:17.332
In this section, we will check the reading order in a PDF.

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:22.033
Reading order is important because it tells

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:25.133
assistive technologies like screen readers

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:28.466
what to read first, second, and so on.

00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:31.266
If the order is incorrect, the content may read

00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:34.632
out of sequence, making it confusing for learners.

00:01:35.366 --> 00:01:37.399
To check reading order,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:41.033
open the Order panel from the right side panel.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.233
Expand the page to view the numbered items.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.500
'1' is the first item read by a screen reader,

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:50.666
'2' is next, and so on.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.900
You cannot edit reading order directly here,

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.733
but you can fix it in the Tags panel.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.700
In this section, we will add tags to give the PDF

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.700
a clear structure.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.133
Tags are hidden labels that identify the structure

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:12.333
of your document, such as headings, paragraphs,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:13.966
lists,

00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:17.033
tables,

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.500
sections.

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:21.932
These tags help assistive

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:25.733
technology understand how the document is organized.

00:02:25.733 --> 00:02:28.866
To view and edit tags, right-click on

00:02:28.866 --> 00:02:31.599
the side panel and make sure Tags is selected.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.500
Open the Tags panel.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.933
Expand the tags to see how each element is labeled.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.833
In this example, my headings are incorrectly

00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:46.666
tagged as paragraphs.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.966
Here is how to fix them.

00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:55.732
Right-click the P tag. Select Properties. Under

00:02:55.733 --> 00:02:59.733
Type, change it to Heading Level 1 or the

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:03.499
appropriate level. Repeat for all headings to

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.066
ensure that they are correctly tagged.

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.866
In this section, we will add alternative text to

00:03:24.866 --> 00:03:25.466
images.

00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:30.033
Any meaningful image in your PDF should include

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:33.433
alternative text that explain its purpose, not

00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:37.099
just what it looks like. To begin adding alt text,

00:03:37.766 --> 00:03:43.266
right-click the Figure tag. Select Properties. Enter

00:03:43.266 --> 00:03:45.632
your description in the Alternative Text field.

00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:49.399
An example of alternative text for this image

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.800
would be "Smiling teacher sitting with the student

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.000
working on a laptop showing collaboration and

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.733
growth." Click Close.

00:04:03.933 --> 00:04:06.799
In this section, we will run the Accessibility

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.500
Checker and do a quick manual review for

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.733
accessibility. Let's identify any additional

00:04:13.733 --> 00:04:18.266
accessibility issues in our document. Go to All

00:04:18.266 --> 00:04:24.299
Tools, then Prepare for Accessibility, then Check

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.500
for Accessibility. Make sure all options are

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.600
selected; then click Start Checking. Review the

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.633
results in the Accessibility Checker panel. Some

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:42.033
items like reading order and color contrast always

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:46.266
require manual review. After checking manually,

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.966
you can right-click and select Pass.

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:53.366
Finally, save your document.
